In a #small bowl{}, wash and drain @rice{1%cup}(uncooked white, i.e. Jasmine). Then add @water{4%cups} and @cinnamon sticks{2}(broken up into smaller pieces, or alternatively 1 tbsp cinnamon). Cover and refrigerate overnight, or at least for ~{4%hours}.

In a #blender, blend the rice, water, and cinnamon sticks in separate batches. Puree until it's very smooth and forms a paste-like texture, about ~{4%minutes} per batch.

Using a #cheese cloth{}, pour the blended mixture into a #pitcher{}. Repeat until all mixture is transferred.

Stir in @evaporated milk{12%oz can}, @sweetened condensed milk{12%oz can}, @?vanilla{1/2%teaspoon}, and the additional @water{4%cups}. Stir well until everything is incorporated.

Taste and add sugar and cinnamon or more water if needed according to taste.

Chill and stir before serving over ice.

Top with cinnamon or additional cinnamon sticks as desired.

> For a boozy variant, add some rum to make Rumchata.